      "description": "Watch Bolton Wanderers vs Preston North End highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The Championship clash between Bolton Wanderers and Preston North End on August 15, 2026, delivered a tactical battle filled with intensity and late-game heroics. Fans at the Toughsheet Community Stadium witnessed a match defined by momentum shifts and a relentless pursuit of three points by both sides. Early Breakthrough and Rapid Response The match ignited early as the hosts looked to establish dominance. In the 14th minute, Sam Dalby found the back of the net to give Bolton Wanderers a 1-0 lead, capitalizing on a period of sustained pressure. This opening goal followed a cagey start where Preston North End 's Alistair McCann had already seen yellow for a heavy challenge. However, the lead proved short-lived. Preston regrouped quickly and began to find gaps in the Bolton defense. Their persistence paid off in the 25th minute when John McAtee turned provider, setting up Thierry Gale for a clinical finish that leveled the score. As the first half progressed, the game turned into a physical battle, with the referee busy issuing cautions to Jordan Thompson and Pol Valentin to keep emotions in check before the break. Erabi’s Late Impact Changes the Narrative The second half began with similar grit, as Bolton 's Josh Sheehan was booked shortly after the restart. Both managers turned to their benches to find a spark, with Thierry Gale making way for Kyliane Dong and Jusef Erabi replacing Callum Lang . These tactical adjustments shifted the balance of play as the match entered its closing stages. In the 86th minute, the decisive moment arrived. Super-sub Jusef Erabi silenced the home crowd, finishing a well-placed pass from Andrija Vukcevic to put Preston ahead. Despite a late yellow card for Bolton 's Chris Forino-Joseph and frantic attempts to equalize in stoppage time, Preston North End held their nerve to secure a vital victory on the road."
